::MCR_U02_L05_GuidedPractice_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U02_L05_GuidedPractice_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.AR.5
Question:
A savings account starts with $400 and grows by 5% each year. Which model represents the balance after t years?
{
~A. A \= 400(0.05)ᵗ#This uses the percent as the factor. Growth keeps 100% and adds 5%, so the factor is 1.05.
=B. A \= 400(1.05)ᵗ#Correct. The initial value is 400 and the 5% growth factor is 1.05.
~C. A \= 1.05(400)ᵗ#This puts the initial value in the exponent position, which does not match the model.
~D. A \= 400 + 5t#This is linear addition, not exponential growth by a repeated factor.
}
::MCR_U02_L05_GuidedPractice_Q02::
Question ID: MCR_U02_L05_GuidedPractice_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.AR.5
Question:
A car worth $18,000 loses 10% of its value each year. What is the decay factor?
{
~A. 0.10#This is the percent lost, not the amount remaining after the loss.
~B. 1.10#This would represent 10% growth, not decay.
=C. 0.90#Correct. After losing 10%, 90% remains, so the decay factor is 0.90.
~D. 10#This uses the percent as a whole number instead of a factor.
}
::MCR_U02_L05_GuidedPractice_Q03::
Question ID: MCR_U02_L05_GuidedPractice_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.AR.5
Question:
Evaluate A = 200(1.10)².
{
~A. $220#This applies 10% growth only once.
~B. $240#This adds 20% directly, but compounding multiplies by 1.10 twice.
~C. $400#This doubles the starting amount without using the growth factor.
=D. $242#Correct. 1.10² = 1.21, and 200 times 1.21 is 242.
}
::MCR_U02_L05_GuidedPractice_Q04::
Question ID: MCR_U02_L05_GuidedPractice_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.AR.5
Question:
Which situation is best modeled exponentially?
{
=A. A plant doubles in height each week#Correct. Doubling each week means repeated multiplication.
~B. A worker earns $15 per hour#This is a constant hourly rate, so it is linear.
~C. A taxi charges $5 plus $2 per mile#This has a constant additive change, so it is linear.
~D. A parking garage charges a flat fee#A flat fee does not show repeated multiplication.
}
::MCR_U02_L05_GuidedPractice_Q05::
Question ID: MCR_U02_L05_GuidedPractice_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.AR.5
Question:
In A = 750(0.92)ᵗ, what does 750 represent?
{
~A. The decay factor#The decay factor is 0.92.
=B. The initial value#Correct. The initial value is the starting amount before any time passes.
~C. The number of years#The exponent t represents the number of time periods.
~D. The percent decrease#The percent decrease is related to 0.92, which means an 8% decrease.
}